0:{"buildId":"7afh9cBoHBO9HIwX4Lcyt","data":[{"rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[["$","$L2",null,{"toc":[{"depth":2,"url":"#the-diode","title":"The diode"},{"depth":2,"url":"#what-crosses-the-boundary-and-what-doesnt","title":"What crosses the boundary and what doesn't"},{"depth":2,"url":"#run-both-while-you-cut-over","title":"Run both while you cut over"},{"depth":2,"url":"#steps","title":"Steps"},{"depth":2,"url":"#when-it-doesnt-work","title":"When it doesn't work"}],"children":[["$","$L3",null,{"children":"Migrate from another REAPI cache"}],["$","$L4",null,{"children":"Put Forge in front of your existing cache as a read-only diode, let real builds warm it, and cut over when the hit rate says you can."}],["$","$L5",null,{"children":["\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Who this is for:"}]," anyone running Buildbarn, Buildfarm, bazel-remote or a\nhosted REAPI cache who wants to move to Forge without a flag day. ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"What\nyou'll have at the end:"}]," Forge serving your builds, backed by the old\ncache, with a cutover you choose rather than one you're forced into. ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"Time:"}],"\nan hour to set up; days to weeks of running both, at your pace."]}],"\n",["$","div",null,{"data-prerequisites":true,"className":"my-6 rounded-xl border border-border bg-surface-elevated px-5 py-3","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"my-0 font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-brand","children":"Before you start"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-1 text-sm text-muted-foreground [&>p]:my-0","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["A working Forge CAS. See ",["$","$L6",null,{"href":"/getting-started","children":"Getting started"}],"."]}]}]]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"The instinct is to copy the data across. Don't. A remote cache is not a\ndatabase: every entry in it is derived, reproducible, and has a key that is a\nhash of its own contents. Copying terabytes to preserve something your build can\nregenerate is work you can skip."}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"The move that works instead is to put Forge in front of the old cache and\nlet it read through. Builds hit Forge; anything it doesn't have, it fetches\nfrom the old cache and keeps. Your hit rate never drops, the new cache warms\nitself on real traffic, and the old one is never written to again, so if you\nneed to go back, it is exactly as you left it."}],"\n",["$","a",null,{"href":"https://github.com/toxicwind/forge/blob/v1.6.5/forge-config/src/stores.rs","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","data-source-link":"forge-config/src/stores.rs","data-source-ref":"v1.6.5","title":"forge-config/src/stores.rs at v1.6.5","className":"inline-flex items-center gap-1 rounded-md border border-border bg-surface-elevated px-1.5 py-0.5 align-middle font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground no-underline transition-colors hover:border-brand/50 hover:text-brand","children":[["$","svg",null,{"width":"12","height":"12","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","aria-hidden":"true","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"m16 18 6-6-6-6M8 6l-6 6 6 6"}]}],"GrpcSpec"]}],"\n",["$","$L7",null,{"as":"h2","id":"the-diode","children":"The diode"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["A ",["$","code",null,{"children":"fast_slow"}]," store whose ",["$","code",null,{"children":"slow"}]," half points at the old cache, marked read-only:"]}],"\n",["$","$L8",null,{"className":"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark","style":{"--shiki-light":"#24292e","--shiki-dark":"#e1e4e8","--shiki-light-bg":"#fff","--shiki-dark-bg":"#24292e"},"tabIndex":"0","icon":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M 6,1 C 4.354992,1 3,2.354992 3,4 v 16 c 0,1.645008 1.354992,3 3,3 h 12 c 1.645008,0 3,-1.354992 3,-3 V 8 7 A 1.0001,1.0001 0 0 0 20.707031,6.2929687 l -5,-5 A 1.0001,1.0001 0 0 0 15,1 h -1 z m 0,2 h 7 v 3 c 0,1.645008 1.354992,3 3,3 h 3 v 11 c 0,0.564