10:["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Digests must match."}]," If your old cache holds SHA-256 entries and your\nbuilds now ask for BLAKE3, nothing is found, not because of a bug but because\nthe key of a blob is its hash, and you are asking a different question. The\ndigest function is chosen by the client (Bazel's ",["$","code",null,{"children":"--digest_function"}],", SHA-256\nunless you changed it); Forge's ",["$","code",null,{"children":"global.default_digest_hash_function"}],",\ndescribed in ",["$","$L6",null,{"href":"/configuration/stores","children":"Stores"}],", only fills in when a client does\nnot say. Keep the client, Forge and the old cache on the same function.\nThis is the one incompatibility that cannot be worked around."]}]
11:["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Instance names may need rewriting."}]," ",["$","code",null,{"children":"instance_name"}]," on the ",["$","code",null,{"children":"grpc"}]," store\nreplaces the instance name on every proxied call, so an old cache that expects\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"main"}]," while your clients send an empty instance is a one-field fix rather than\na client migration."]}]
12:["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Older backends want older resource names."}]," Modern REAPI resource names look\nlike ",["$","code",null,{"children":"{instance}/blobs/{digest_function}/{hash}/{size}"}],". Buildbarn before v0.3\nand other older servers expect the original ",["$","code",null,{"children":"{instance}/blobs/{hash}/{size}"}],", and\nsending them the modern form produces ",["$","code",null,{"children":"InvalidArgument: Unsupported digest function"}],". Set ",["$","code",null,{"children":"use_legacy_resource_names: true"}]," when you see that."]}]
