21:["$","$L42",null,{"children":[["$","$L43",null,{"title":"Everything misses: the diode returns nothing","id":"everything-misses--the-diode-returns-nothing","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["Check the digest function first; a mismatch produces exactly this and no error.\nThen check ",["$","code",null,{"children":"instance_name"}],", since an old cache scoped to a named instance\nreturns nothing for a differently-named one. Then confirm the address is\nreachable from the Forge process rather than from your laptop."]}]}],["$","$L43",null,{"title":"`InvalidArgument: Unsupported digest function`","id":"invalidargument-unsupported-digest-function","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["The upstream is an older server that does not understand modern resource names.\nSet ",["$","code",null,{"children":"use_legacy_resource_names: true"}]," on the ",["$","code",null,{"children":"grpc"}]," store."]}]}],["$","$L43",null,{"title":"The old cache is getting writes","id":"the-old-cache-is-getting-writes","children":["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","code",null,{"children":"slow_direction"}]," is not set to ",["$","code",null,{"children":"read_only"}],", or it is set on the wrong store. It\nbelongs on the ",["$","code",null,{"children":"fast_slow"}]," wrapper next to ",["$","code",null,{"children":"slow"}],", not inside the ",["$","code",null,{"children":"grpc"}]," spec.\nIts default is ",["$","code",null,{"children":"both"}],", which is a normal read-write tier."]}]}],["$","$L43",null,{"title":"Large blobs fail partway through the diode","id":"large-blobs-fail-partway-through-the-diode","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["A per-RPC timeout. Set ",["$","code",null,{"children":"rpc_timeout_s: 0"}]," on the ",["$","code",null,{"children":"grpc"}]," store (the default),\nor raise it well past the worst-case transfer time. Multi-gigabyte blobs\npulled cross-region are slower than any guess."]}]}],["$","$L43",null,{"title":"Hit rate is good but builds got slower","id":"hit-rate-is-good-but-builds-got-slower","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["Every miss now costs a round trip to the old cache on top of the local lookup.\nThat is the diode working as designed and it is temporary. If it is painful,\nraise the local store's ",["$","code",null,{"children":"max_bytes"}]," so fewer reads fall through, and check\nwhether the old cache is in another region."]}]}],["$","$L43",null,{"title":"Should I ever actually copy the data?","id":"should-i-ever-actually-copy-the-data","children":["$","p",null,{"children":"Rarely, and only when the old cache holds artifacts that are expensive or\nimpossible to reproduce: a toolchain nobody can rebuild, or outputs from a\nsource revision that no longer exists. That is a one-off copy of specific blobs,\nnot a migration strategy. For everything a build can regenerate, the diode is\nboth faster and safer."}]}]]}]
